MID_SE_Seo_Led_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_001: Hm. That horse approaches swiftly. And I can now\nmake out its rider...
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_002: Whoa, girl. Oh, Queen Theodora. Hello.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_003: Greetings, Leda. On an urgent errand, I take it?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_004: Not really. I just thought I'd take a nice long ride.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_005: This girl has lots of energy to burn, and I love how\nthe wind feels on my face when she really gets going.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_006: Hah. I'm unaccustomed to seeing you wear\na genuine smile.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_007: I'm not sure what you mean.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_008: Whether to control the situation or to protect\nyourself, you often keep your emotions in check.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_009: It seems to take the presence of a horse for you to\nlet slip an honest smile.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_010: I don't know about that...
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_011: But I admit this girl does make it hard not to smile.\nHere, take her to a gallop—you'll see.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_012: You noble types seem fond of riding, so I'm sure\nyou'll appreciate her spirit.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_013: What? No...I have never been "fond of riding."
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_014: Go ahead, she's all yours. Off you go!
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_015: Gyaaah!
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_016: Haaah... Haaah... And what is so funny, may I ask?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_017: I'm sorry, Queen Theodora. It's just, I've never seen\nyou so NOT in control. It was adorable.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_018: I'll admit though, it was surprising to see a noble like\nyourself ride a horse so...awkwardly.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_019: I know a warrior's rudiments of riding. So long as\nthere are no sudden surprises.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_020: A queen reigns from a palanquin or her throne.\nWhat need has she of horse mastery?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_021: I see. Well, I've been riding horses since I was a\nchild, so I've had lots of time to hone my skills.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_022: Growing up, I would ride as far and fast as I could,\nwatching the landscape of Cydonia fly by...
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_023: Ah...
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_024: Is something wrong? Do you find it unpleasant to\nthink upon your home?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_025: It's nothing. It's just time I return this horse.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_026: Perhaps she longs for Cydonia even now.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_B_027: She is blessed with talent and longs for home, yet she\nis still so hesitant. Hm.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_001: Leda! Shall we ride across the countryside together?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_002: You want to ride horses...with me? I thought you\ndidn't enjoy riding.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_003: Worry not on my account. It is a pretext for the\ntwo of us to speak.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_004: Ah, I see. In that case, I'll take you to one of my\nfavorite spots.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_005: This is it, Queen Theodora. I hope you like it.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_006: I can see why you love it here. It must have been\nhard to find, given the state of the world.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_007: Actually, I was out on one of my long rides when\nI came across it.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_008: Speaking of which, I'm surprised to see how much\nyour own horseback skills have improved.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_009: I see what's going on. You started practicing just so\nyou could go riding with me. Come on, admit it.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_010: Your conclusion is correct.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_011: Wait...what? I...I was just teasing.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_012: I envy your skill at riding. Who taught you?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_013: My father did. But that was a long time ago.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_014: I have been meaning to ask...have you any interest\nin reclaiming your status in Cydonia?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_015: The people would surely welcome your return. None\ncan deny your noble blood.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_016: No...I do not. Besides, there's nothing left of\nHouse Cohendia.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_017: I see no issue there. You have the stature to lead\narmies already.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_018: You are adored far and wide. The sound of your\nvihuela inspires all who hear it.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_019: When I play my vihuela, I'm not trying to\ninspire anyone.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_020: I just want those soldiers to fight well on my behalf\nso I have a better chance of surviving. That's all.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_021: I'm not doing anything for them. I'm just...\nusing them.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_022: True enough. And what of it?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_023: I don't...understand.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_024: You reign by spurring on your soldiers as best you\ncan. What leader could not say the same?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_025: You approve of what I'm doing? Why do you care\nso much?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_026: There is great talent in you. I will not sit idly by as\nyou waste it convincing yourself otherwise.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_027: Moreover, it is obvious that you still care\nfor Cydonia.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_028: Ah...
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_029: I fully believe you are worthy to rule your homeland.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_030: You're a queen...
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_031: When you say things like that, I want to believe you.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_032: Be that as it may, our war is not yet won.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_033: When you have made up your mind, I will be there\nto encourage you once more.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_034: After another ride across the plains side by side,\nof course.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_035: I'd like that. But how will you find the time to go\nriding with me after you return to your country?
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_036: Heh. Who will stop me? Everyone knows how fond\nnobles are of this sort of thing.
MID_SE_Seo_Led_A_037: Hehe. We really are, aren't we?